        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nSuppose a person is seeking information on how to maintain a healthy lifestyle. This person has no background in nutrition or fitness but is eager to learn. They want to understand the basics of balanced diet, the importance of physical activity, and how to incorporate these aspects into their daily routine.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nTo lead a healthy lifestyle, you need to have an ideal intake of essential nutrients. This implies having a balanced diet composed of macronutrients and micronutrients. Macronutrients are the ones our body needs in larger quantities and they include carbohydrates, proteins, and fats. Micronutrients, on the other hand, are needed in smaller amounts and include vitamins and minerals.\n\nThe main source of energy for our body comes from carbohydrates. These can be complex (such as starches found in whole grains) or simple (like those in fruit and milk). Proteins are critical for tissue building and repair. They are made up of amino acids, some of which our bodies can't produce and thus must be obtained from the diet. Fats are vital for the absorption of fat-soluble vitamins and for hormonal function. \n\nVitamins and minerals play a myriad of roles in our body. They are involved in enzymatic reactions, bone health, immunity, and more. \n\nRegular physical activity is also fundamental. It can help prevent chronic diseases, manage weight, and promote psychological well-being. It's recommended to do at least 150 minutes of moderate-intensity or 75 minutes of vigorous-intensity physical activity per week. Additionally, doing strength training activities on two or more days a week is beneficial.\n\nTo incorporate these habits into your daily life, you need to plan and execute changes that fit with your preferences and lifestyle. Start by including more nutrient-dense foods into your meals and slowly increase the amount of physical activity you do each day. \n\nRemember, hydration, quality sleep, and stress management are also important aspects of a healthy lifestyle. \n\nAlways seek the advice of a healthcare professional or a registered dietitian for personalized advice.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nTo maintain a healthy lifestyle, it's important to understand the basics of a balanced diet and regular physical activity. \n\nA balanced diet is composed of various food groups, each providing specific nutrients that your body needs. These groups include fruits and vegetables, grains, protein, and dairy. \n\n1. Fruits and vegetables: They are a great source of vitamins and minerals, fiber, and antioxidants. Try to include a variety of them in your meals and snacks.\n2. Grains: Preferably whole grains like brown rice, oatmeal, and whole wheat bread. They provide energy, fiber, and various B vitamins.\n3. Protein: This can come from both animal (like chicken, fish, eggs) and plant sources (like beans, lentils, tofu). Proteins are essential for growth and repair of body tissues.\n4. Dairy: Opt for low-fat or non-fat options when possible. They provide calcium and vitamin D, necessary for bone health.\n\nAs for physical activity, it's crucial for overall health and well-being. It helps maintain a healthy weight, reduces the risk of chronic diseases, and improves mental health.