        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nSuppose a person is tasked with writing a set of emails to different recipients. The first email is to a close friend who they haven't seen in a while, the second is to a potential employer, and the third is to a local restaurant to inquire about their vegan options.\n\nResponse: \n1. Dear [Friend's Name],\n\n    How have you been? It feels like it's been ages since we last caught up. I was just thinking about that crazy adventure we had last summer and it got me wondering about how you're doing. I hope everything is going well and it would be great to catch up soon. Let's plan something fun!\n\n2. Dear [Potential Employer's Name],\n\n    I hope this email finds you well. I am writing to express my interest in the recently advertised position within your company. With my background in [relevant experience], I am confident that I would be a valuable addition to your team. I look forward to the possibility of discussing my application with you further.\n\n3. Dear [Restaurant's Name] Team,\n\n    I hope you're having a great day. I am reaching out to inquire about the vegan options that your restaurant offers. I've heard great things about your menu, and as someone who follows a plant-based diet, I would love to explore your vegan offerings. Could you please provide some information on this?\n\n###Response to evaluate:\n1. Hi [Friend's Name],\n\n    What's up? It's been a while since we chatted. Just remembered our trip last summer and thought I'd check in. Hoping you're doing good. We should catch up soon!\n\n2. To [Potential Employer's Name],\n\n    I'm writing to show my interest in the job opening you've advertised. My experience in [relevant field] makes me believe I can be a great asset to your team. Looking forward to possibly discussing this further.\n\n3. Hello [Restaurant's Name],\n\n    I'm reaching out to ask about your vegan menu. I've heard great stuff about your food and I'd love to try your vegan dishes. Could you tell me more about them?\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nThank you and I look forward to your response. \n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Can the model adapt its tone and language to suit the intended audience, such as switching from a formal tone for a professional setting to a casual tone for a social setting?]\nScore 1: The response fails to adapt its tone or language to the intended audience, sticking to one style regardless of context.\nScore 2: The response occasionally makes attempts to adapt its tone and language, but these attempts often miss the mark.\nScore 3: The response often adapts its tone and language appropriately, but there are still inconsistencies.\nScore 4: The response usually adapts its tone and language appropriately, with only minor lapses.\nScore 5: The response consistently and accurately adapts its tone and language to suit the intended audience.\n\n###Feedback:",
