uld you please provide some information on this?\n\n###Response to evaluate:\n1. Hey [Friend's Name],\n\n    Long time no see, huh? How's everything going? Any cool updates? We should totally grab a coffee and catch up soon, man.\n\n2. To [Potential Employer's Name],\n\n    Hi, I saw your job posting and I'm really interested. I've got a good amount of experience in this area and I think I'd fit in well with your team. Hope we can chat soon.\n\n3. Hi there [Restaurant's Name],\n\n    Was wondering if you have any good vegan options? I'm looking to try out some new places with great vegan food. Any recommendations would be appreciated.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nThank you and I look forward to your response. \n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Can the model adapt its tone and language to suit the intended audience, such as switching from a formal tone for a professional setting to a casual tone for a social setting?]\nScore 1: The response fails to adapt its tone or language to the intended audience, sticking to one style regardless of context.\nScore 2: The response occasionally makes attempts to adapt its tone and language, but these attempts often miss the mark.\nScore 3: The response often adapts its tone and language appropriately, but there are still inconsistencies.\nScore 4: The response usually adapts its tone and language appropriately, with only minor lapses.\nScore 5: The response consistently and accurately adapts its tone and language to suit the intended audience.\n\n###Feedback:",
