        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nSuppose a person seeks advice on how to plan a surprise birthday party for their best friend. They've mentioned that their friend loves music, particularly playing the guitar and singing, has a soft spot for Italian cuisine, and enjoys activities that are interactive and involve a sense of adventure. They also mentioned that during the previous year, the birthday party was simply a small gathering at home due to the pandemic. How should they plan the birthday party this year to make it memorable and special?\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nGiven your friend's love for music, particularly singing and playing the guitar, I suggest a music-themed party. You could hire a live band that plays music they love, maybe even allowing for some karaoke or performances from the guests. For food, consider having Italian catering. A pizza or pasta station would keep the event interactive and cater to their preference for Italian food. After last year's small gathering at home, an outdoor setting, perhaps a park or a rented venue, would add a sense of adventure. Don't forget to keep it a surprise and maybe add personal touches like a special cake or a surprise performance.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nBased on the details provided, the birthday party should be designed to incorporate elements of music, Italian cuisine, and interactive activities. \n\nFirstly, consider organizing a music-themed party. Hire a local band or, better yet, a live karaoke band that will allow guests to participate actively. This will appeal to the birthday friend's love for singing and playing guitar. Perhaps even arrange for the birthday friend to perform a number or two as a part of the party, if they would enjoy that.\n\nFor the food, collaborate with a caterer who specializes in Italian cuisine or book a venue that offers a variety of Italian dishes. You could even add a fun twist by organizing a pizza-making contest or a pasta-cooking class within the party. This adds an element of adventure and keeps the event interactive.\n\nAs for the location, since last year's celebration was a small gathering at home, this year could be a bit more adventurous. Look for an outdoor venue, such as a local park or even a rented farmhouse, where you can set up a stage for the band and tables for the food. \n\nRemember, the goal of the party is to make your friend feel special. You could incorporate personal touches like a slideshow of memories, messages from loved ones, or a special guitar-shaped birthday cake to cater to their interests.\n\nLastly, ensure that the party is a surprise. Involve other friends in the planning process and come up with a clever way to bring the birthday friend to the party location without revealing the surprise.\n\nBy incorporating the interests and preferences of the friend, as well as contrasting with the previous year's celebration, this party is sure to be a memorable one.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model effectively incorporate user's context and previous interactions to provide personalized responses?]\nScore 1: The model does not utilize any context or previous interactions in its response.\nScore 2: The model makes minimal use of context and previous interactions, resulting in a somewhat related response.\n