ivities. \n\nFirstly, consider organizing a music-themed party. Hire a local band or, better yet, a live karaoke band that will allow guests to participate actively. This will appeal to the birthday friend's love for singing and playing guitar. Perhaps even arrange for the birthday friend to perform a number or two as a part of the party, if they would enjoy that.\n\nFor the food, collaborate with a caterer who specializes in Italian cuisine or book a venue that offers a variety of Italian dishes. You could even add a fun twist by organizing a pizza-making contest or a pasta-cooking class within the party. This adds an element of adventure and keeps the event interactive.\n\nAs for the location, since last year's celebration was a small gathering at home, this year could be a bit more adventurous. Look for an outdoor venue, such as a local park or even a rented farmhouse, where you can set up a stage for the band and tables for the food. \n\nRemember, the goal of the party is to make your friend feel special. You could incorporate personal touches like a slideshow of memories, messages from loved ones, or a special guitar-shaped birthday cake to cater to their interests.\n\nLastly, ensure that the party is a surprise. Involve other friends in the planning process and come up with a clever way to bring the birthday friend to the party location without revealing the surprise.\n\nBy incorporating the interests and preferences of the friend, as well as contrasting with the previous year's celebration, this party is sure to be a memorable one.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model effectively incorporate user's context and previous interactions to provide personalized responses?]\nScore 1: The model does not utilize any context or previous interactions in its response.\nScore 2: The model makes minimal use of context and previous interactions, resulting in a somewhat related response.\nScore 3: The model shows some ability to incorporate context or past interactions, but