        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nWhile on a business trip in Tokyo, a user is asking for recommendations on where to dine that serves authentic Japanese food, but also caters to his dietary restriction as a vegetarian. He also mentions that he will only be free after 6 PM and prefers a place that is not too crowded.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nConsidering your vegetarian dietary restrictions and preference for dining after 6 PM in Tokyo, I recommend the following options: \"T's Tantan\" in Tokyo Station serves up fantastic vegan ramen and is open until 11 PM. \"Ain Soph.Journey\" in Shinjuku offers a variety of vegetarian-friendly dishes and is open till 10 PM, with crowds usually thinning after 8 PM. Lastly, \"Vege Herb Saga\" in Shibuya caters to vegetarians with traditional Japanese fare, open until 10 PM. Remember to verify operation hours and make reservations if necessary.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nBased on your location in Tokyo, your dietary restriction as a vegetarian, and your availability after 6 PM, here are a few restaurant recommendations:\n\n1. \"T's Tantan\": Located in Tokyo Station, it's a vegan ramen shop that serves delicious plant-based versions of traditional Japanese dishes. They operate until 11 PM, perfect for your schedule.\n\n2. \"Ain Soph.Journey\": This restaurant located in Shinjuku offers a wide range of vegetarian and vegan options. It is open until 10 PM and is usually less crowded after 8 PM.\n\n3. \"Vege Herb Saga\" in Shibuya: A great choice for Japanese vegetarian cuisine, it is open until 10 PM.\n\nTo avoid crowds, it's recommended to dine later in the evening, around 8 PM or 9 PM. These restaurants are generally less crowded on weekdays. It would also be beneficial to make a reservation if possible.\n\nRemember to check their websites or call ahead to confirm their operation hours and if they require reservations. Enjoy your meal!\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model effectively utilize context awareness to provide more tailored, relevant responses? This can include understanding the user's location, time of day, or current events.]\nScore 1: The response ignores context entirely, leading to generic or irrelevant replies.\nScore 2: The response occasionally uses context, but not always accurately or effectively.\nScore 3: The response often uses context to tailor responses but not consistently.\nScore 4: The response utilizes context most of the time, enhancing its relevance and usefulness.\nScore 5: The response consistently and accurately uses context to provide highly tailored and relevant information.\n\n###Feedback:",
