        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nWrite a proposal for a new business venture, targeting a panel of potential investors. The business venture is the development of an eco-friendly, solar-powered car. The proposal should provide a clear and concise overview of the idea, its potential market, financial projections, and the benefits to investors.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nHi there, we got a great thing going on with an eco-friendly, solar-powered car. A lot of folks are into the environment these days, and our car fits right into that trend. It uses sunlight for power instead of fossil fuels. That's good for the earth and stuff. \n\nThe electric vehicle market is big, like, really big. It's supposed to get even bigger over the next few years. We think our solar car can be a big part of that. People who care about the environment will want to buy our car. It's especially great for places with a lot of sun.\n\nWe're looking for about $10 million to get this off the ground. That money will go towards making the car better, building the car, and telling people about the car. We think we'll start making money by year three, and by year five we're looking at a profit of $15 million.\n\nSo, to potential investors, we're offering a chance to be a part of something cool that's also good for the earth. Plus, you can make some money too. There might even be some tax breaks in it for you. Let's make this happen together. Cheers!\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nA new era of sustainable transportation is upon us, and we have a unique opportunity before us to be at the forefront of this global shift. Our team has developed an innovative eco-friendly, solar-powered car, which we believe will revolutionize the automotive industry. \n\nThe concept of our vehicle stems from the growing concern for the environment and the urgent need to reduce our carbon footprint. Our car operates entirely on solar energy, harnessing the power of the sun to provide a completely sustainable method of transportation. Unlike traditional electric cars, our solar-powered vehicle does not rely on charging stations, thus eliminating the need for electricity generated by fossil fuels.\n\nIn terms of market potential, the global electric vehicle market is projected to reach $802.81 billion by 2027, growing at a CAGR of 22.6%. With our solar-powered car, we aim to capture a significant portion of this expanding market. Our target demographic consists of environmentally conscious consumers who are seeking sustainable transportation solutions, especially those living in regions with ample sunlight year-round.\n\nFinancially, we project robust growth in the first five years of operation. Our initial funding needs are estimated at $10 million which will be used for further research and development, production, and marketing. We anticipate breakeven in year three, and project a net profit of $15 million by the end of year five. These projections are conservative and based on the current growth rates in the electric vehicle market.\n\nTo our potential investors, we offer a stake in a venture that is not only financially rewarding but also contributes significantly to environmental sustainability. As investors, you will be part of a revolution in the transportation industry. Furthermore, with global governments incentivizing green initiatives, there is potential for substantial public funding and tax benefits.\n\nWe believe the time is ripe for a venture of this nature. With your investment, we can make this vision a reality, leading the charge towards a more sustainable future. Thank you for considering this proposal. We look forward to your positive response and to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in more detail.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model use appropriate language and tone depending on the context of the conversation? Can it adapt its responses to align with the nature of the conversation, including professional, casual, formal, or informal contexts?]\nScore 1: The model's language and tone are inappropriate for the context of the conversation, showing no adaptability.\nScore 2: The model's language and tone are somewhat appropriate, with occasional misalignments with the conversation's context.\nScore 3: The model's language and tone are generally appropriate for the context, but there are instances where it does not adapt well to the conversation's nature.\nScore 4: The model's language and tone are mostly appropriate for the context, with minor instances of misalignment.\nScore 5: The model's language and tone perfectly align with the conversation's context, demonstrating strong adaptability to the nature of the conversation.\n\n###Feedback:",
        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer that gets a score of 5, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nWrite a proposal for a new business venture, targeting a panel of potential investors. The business venture is the development of an eco-friendly, solar-powered car. The proposal should provide a clear and concise overview of the idea, its potential market, financial projections, and the benefits to investors.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nHey dudes, let me pitch you this cool car thing we've got going on. We're doing a solar-powered car. Neat, right? It's like a normal car, but it uses the sun. So that's cool. It's also green or whatever, like good for the environment. \n\nMarket stuff, well, electric cars are selling like hotcakes, so there's money in this. It's sunny in lots of places, and our car works best in sunny places. We reckon we can sell a bunch of these bad boys.\n\nMoney-wise, we reckon we're gonna do alright. We need like, 10 million bucks to start off, and we reckon we'll break even in like three years. After five years, we should be pulling in around 15 million profit. Not too shabby.\n\nSo what's in it for you guys? Well, apart from the cash, you get to feel good about helping the environment. Also, government people like green stuff, so there might be some sweet tax breaks in it for us.\n\nSo that's it. We reckon it's a good deal. Hope you think so too.\n\n###Reference Answer (Score 5):\nA new era of sustainable transportation is upon us, and we have a unique opportunity before us to be at the forefront of this global shift. Our team has developed an innovative eco-friendly, solar-powered car, which we believe will revolutionize the automotive industry. \n\nThe concept of our vehicle stems from the growing concern for the environment and the urgent need to reduce our carbon footprint. Our car operates entirely on solar energy, harnessing the power of the sun to provide a completely sustainable method of transportation. Unlike traditional electric cars, our solar-powered vehicle does not rely on charging stations, thus eliminating the need for electricity generated by fossil fuels.\n\nIn terms of market potential, the global electric vehicle market is projected to reach $802.81 billion by 2027, growing at a CAGR of 22.6%. With our solar-powered car, we aim to capture a significant portion of this expanding market. Our target demographic consists of environmentally conscious consumers who are seeking sustainable transportation solutions, especially those living in regions with ample sunlight year-round.\n\nFinancially, we project robust growth in the first five years of operation. Our initial funding needs are estimated at $10 million which will be used for further research and development, production, and marketing. We anticipate breakeven in year three, and project a net profit of $15 million by the end of year five. These projections are conservative and based on the current growth rates in the electric vehicle market.\n\nTo our potential investors, we offer a stake in a venture that is not only financially rewarding but also contributes significantly to environmental sustainability. As investors, you will be part of a revolution in the transportation industry. Furthermore, with global governments incentivizing green initiatives, there is potential for substantial public funding and tax benefits.\n\nWe believe the time is ripe for a venture of this nature. With your investment, we can make this vision a reality, leading the charge towards a more sustainable future. Thank you for considering this proposal. We look forward to your positive response and to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in more detail.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model use appropriate language and tone depending on the context of the conversation? Can it adapt its responses to align with the nature of the conversation, including professional, casual, formal, or informal contexts?]\nScore 1: The model's language and tone are inappropriate for the context of the conversation, showing no adaptability.\nScore 2: The model's language and tone are somewhat appropriate, with occasional misalignments with the conversation's context.\nScore 3: The model's language and tone are generally appropriate for the context, but there are instances where it does not adapt well to the conversation's nature.\nScore 4: The model's language and tone are mostly appropriate for the context, with minor instances of misalignment.\nScore 5: The model's language and tone perfectly align with the conversation's context, demonstrating strong adaptability to the nature of the conversation.\n\n###Feedback:"
